From d80a816ec0f5c34953d93daba9fa96b179a43966 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 16:33:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] build: add fastbuild profile for fast edit-compile-test
 iteration

The release profile gained lto="thin" for shipped binaries, which is the
right call for distribution but a disaster for development iteration:
thin LTO disables Cargo's incremental compilation entirely and funnels
all codegen through the serial cross-unit link step. On the 2-core
research box a one-file touch went from seconds to a full multi-minute
rebuild (~4x slower cold, far worse warm).

Add [profile.fastbuild] (inherits release): opt-level=1 (unchanged
project research policy), lto=off, incremental=true, codegen-units=256,
debug=line-tables-only for usable backtraces. Measured on the 2-core
sandbox:

  cold build:            1m24s (fastbuild) - no LTO link stall
  warm rebuild (1 file): 6.3s  (fastbuild) vs minutes under thin LTO

scripts/build_lccc_fast.sh drives it; binaries land in target/fastbuild/.
Test harnesses (correctness, intrinsics, linker) now honor LCCC_BIN so
they can point at either profile; regression/asm-diff already had CCC/
argv overrides. Ship builds unchanged: scripts/build_lccc_o1_j2.sh still
produces the reproducible release-profile artifacts.

PROOF: CCC=./target/fastbuild/lccc tests/regression -> 154/154 PASS.
