From 37031557c98e354e2ac9072554d0ba0e1f14db38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 16:34:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Integrate levkropp AArch64 backend work (commits
 1-16/25), semantically rebased

Semantic (not textual) rebase of Lev's fork onto current main. Every
conflict was resolved by root-cause analysis; where both sides fixed the
same problem the stronger implementation won, where they were orthogonal
both were kept. x86-64 behavior deliberately preserved wherever upstream
had the more hardened variant.

Integrated from levkropp/lccc (in rebase order):
- 835aed29 compiler correctness + AArch64 codegen (bit_idioms pass,
  block_layout, x86 scalar-FP cast/load SSE-domain paths, benchmarks)
- 2b555fbc FP/vector regalloc on AArch64 (v16-v23 pool, allocator IDs
  40..55) + loop-aware inlining (single-call-site static exemption,
  loop-nest-merge guard, leaf-switch-dispatch admission)
- d3ba5c3f madd spilled-operand direct loads
- c835183b FP const hoisting out of loops (fp_const_hoist pass)
- 6243511e CCC_DEBUG_FPCOAL diagnostics
- 8a8c452a (superseded: upstream eviction modes 3/5 with reload support
  are strictly stronger than the documented-unsafe note; kept upstream)
- c107a33a variable-offset GEP -> indexed addressing (IndexedGepInfo,
  supports_indexed_addr/emit_load_indexed/emit_store_indexed trait fns,
  GepOffset::Index liveness extension for base AND index)
- 047b6892 3-channel multiply ILP gated to x86-64
- 8a4d1923 load_forward pass (reload forwarding enables if-conversion)
- 269f07d6 F64x2/I32x4 register-based NEON ops + addv encoding fix
- c16dbc2b VecMulI32x4/VecBroadcastI32x4/VecStoreI32x4 intrinsics
- 160472ec split_ranges (loop-transparent live-range splitting, opt-in)
- afcf62e1 register-direct int-widen casts on AArch64
- af0a2f59 AArch64 register-direct binop rhs-clobber fix
- 006f72f7 post-scan register steal for hot loop-carried phis
  (CCC_LOOP_PIN, AArch64-only, adapted to PhiCoalesceCandidate struct)
- a9cdf1fc loop-backedge phi copy slot coalescing (loop_phi_aliases
  certified bypass of the generic def/last-use interference check)

Key conflict resolutions (perfect-merge decisions):
- vectorize.rs: kept upstream's width-aware remainder-start computation,
  stale-label defense, and F32 support; added Lev's force_two_wide mode
  (vectorize_function_two_wide for AArch64 NEON 128-bit), accumulator_type
  plumbing, and the I32->I64 widening reduction (allow_widening_i32,
  gated so x86 never takes it). AArch64 now runs the 2-wide vectorizer
  in the pass pipeline; x86-64 keeps the 4-wide AVX2 default.
- inline.rs: merged Lev's single-call-site/loop-aware exemptions INTO
  upstream's PGO-force budget structure; both parameter sets unified.
- regalloc.rs: kept upstream's hardened PhiCoalesceCandidate window
  revalidation (fail-closed) and Phase 2c callee-saved overflow; added
  Lev's arm_fp_pool vector/F64 collection, real_use copy-web filter and
  d24..d31 loop-promotion pool; loop-pin steal adapted to the candidate
  struct; non_gpr collection now keys on produces_vector_value() with
  the sqrt/fabs scalar-FP exclusions applied on all targets.
- intrinsics: single source of truth - produces_vector_value() and
  vector_result_width() both extended with the new I64x2/I32x4 families.
- ipcp.rs: kept upstream's bounded constant-call evaluator (subsumes
  Lev's Ackermann/tail-sum structural folds); extended it with
  BitReverse evaluation for Lev's new IrUnaryOp.
- passes/mod.rs: cleanup pipeline gains aggregate_copy_forward,
  loop_memory_promote and cfg_simplify fixed-point stages, each with a
  CCC_NO_* kill switch, ordered before ipcp's evaluator.
- x86 cast_ops/emit/float_ops/memory: register-direct paths kept first
  (dest-register beats staging through xmm0), Lev's broader SSE-domain
  coverage (OverAligned/Indirect FP loads, movapd no-false-dep copies,
  FP-const direct XMM materialization) layered underneath.
- liveness.rs: Lev's extend_one closure structure won (extends BOTH the
  base and the index of a folded indexed access).
- split_ranges.rs: adapted to upstream's semantic_volatile Alloca field.

AArch64-only files (alu/cast_ops/comparison/emit/float_ops/intrinsics/
memory/peephole/prologue, arm linker reloc) taken from Lev verbatim -
orthogonal to x86 by construction.

NOTE: remaining 9 Lev commits (94141751, 90e05e19, 2c3a0d31, 958abd8f,
fef5e2d1, e896ab2b int_const_hoist, 75f5c50a, README/docs rewrites) are
NOT yet integrated - the sandbox toolchain was wiped mid-rebase. Next
session: fetch lev/main, cherry-pick the remainder, then run the full
battery (641 lib tests, 154 regressions, 50 correctness, 86 linker,
240-seed differential fuzz) plus AArch64 cross-validation via
qemu-aarch64 + gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu before any upstream merge.
Compile status: all intermediate states built clean under fastbuild;
the final slot_assignment.rs merge is mechanically trivial but was not
re-compiled after the toolchain wipe - verify first thing next session.
